  "preamble": "Fortition of the voiced bilabial fricative [β] to the stop [b] restores full lip closure. In Old High German the Proto-Germanic medial fricative *β, which survived as [v] in Old English and Old Norse, was hardened to a stop written b, as in *gebaną /ˈɣe.βɑ.nɑ̃/ > gëban /ˈɡɛ.ban/. Latin shows the same hardening in a separate branch: Proto-Italic medial *β, the reflex of PIE *bʰ inside a word, became Latin b, as in *alβos > albus 'white' and *neβelā > nebula 'mist'.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Fortition",
